+/// Largest dimension that is safe to hand to `StripGenerator::new`: the previous multiple of
+/// `Tile::WIDTH`/`Tile::HEIGHT` below `u16::MAX`. `RectU16::snap_to_tile_coordinates` and
+/// `util::strip_bbox` round a rect's `x1`/`y1` up to the next tile multiple and convert back to
+/// pixels via `checked_mul(Tile::WIDTH).unwrap()`; a viewport whose width/height sits in
+/// `(MAX_SAFE_DIMENSION, u16::MAX]` has a partial last tile whose right/bottom edge would need to
+/// be represented as a value beyond `u16::MAX`, so drawing content that reaches into that partial
+/// tile panics. Clamping here keeps every root viewport (including a filter's own padded
+/// viewport, whose width/height derives from a filter's `FilterData::source_padding`, itself
+/// unbounded input scaled by an arbitrary transform - see `FilterData::new`) tile-aligned and
+/// within the range every other user of `RectU16`/tile arithmetic already assumes.
+const MAX_SAFE_DIMENSION: u16 = u16::MAX - (u16::MAX % Tile::WIDTH);
+
 /// Viewport state storing information about clip state and active strip generators in
 /// currently active root viewports.
 #[derive(Debug)]
